{
  "dom_id": "step-q216986",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Expand the following product. Write your answer in **standard form.**\n\n$2{x}^{2}(3{x}^{4}+4)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We multiply each term inside the parentheses by the term outside the parentheses, simplify using the rules of exponents, and then we add the results together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}(3{x}^{4}+4) & = \\\\ 2{x}^{2}\\cdot (3{x}^{4})+2{x}^{2}\\cdot 4 & = \\\\ 6{x}^{2+4}+8{x}^{2} & = \\\\ 6{x}^{6}+8{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
